WEBVTT

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:10.430
Its thirteenth regimental commander 
is Captain Walter von Schönkopf.

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:13.060
Rumors?

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:17.030
Of all their past captains, 
six defected back to the Empire.

00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:19.240
There are concerns that he 
may become the seventh.

00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:23.490
If I become the seventh traitor, 
like the rumors say,

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:26.050
it will be all for naught.

00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:27.830
What would you do then?

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:35.560
Sending our hull number and all crew 
members' personal ID codes.

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:37.820
Awaiting permission to dock.

00:00:42.090 --> 00:00:45.130
Confirmed. Permission to dock received.

00:00:47.510 --> 00:00:50.360
Do you guys have any 
memories of the Empire?

00:00:50.810 --> 00:00:53.390
I'm a second-generation refugee, so no.

00:00:53.390 --> 00:00:56.780
My grandfather came under 
suspicion and was killed.

00:00:56.780 --> 00:00:59.640
I see. That had to be rough.

00:01:00.130 --> 00:01:02.830
I grew up in the Empire until I was six.

00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:06.030
I spent much of my time 
with my grandfather.

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:50.060
<b>Legend of the Galactic Heroes</b>

00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:02.840
Ten minutes have passed since 
the task force entered port.

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:05.370
<u>13th Fleet Flagship
</u>Hyperion

00:03:03.530 --> 00:03:06.340
There has been no request for rescue 
as projected in the event of failure.

00:03:07.630 --> 00:03:11.410
It seems safe to assume they 
succeeded in docking.

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:14.210
We've cleared the first hurdle.

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:15.460
Yes.

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:20.560
If we can clear all the rest of the 
hurdles with the same success,

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:22.370
we'll be in perfect shape.

00:03:26.630 --> 00:03:28.800
I am the captain, 
Lieutenant Commander von Laeken.

00:03:29.170 --> 00:03:31.220
I am Lieutenant Mann, 
captain of the security force.

00:03:31.220 --> 00:03:32.430
What happened out there?

00:03:33.050 --> 00:03:35.960
We were carrying out an espionage mission

00:03:35.960 --> 00:03:38.730
in Alliance territory at Fleet 
Admiral Mückenberger's orders.

00:03:39.270 --> 00:03:42.320
But unfortunately, we were discovered 
and my unit was annihilated.

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:44.870
Amid the chaos, I managed to obtain this,

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:46.620
and only we survived to escape here.

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:49.950
This contains plans for a certain project.

00:03:50.950 --> 00:03:55.620
It appears the rebels came 
up with an unbelievable plan

00:03:55.620 --> 00:03:58.310
to neutralize Iserlohn Fortress 
and pass through the corridor.

00:03:58.310 --> 00:04:00.080
Is that true?

00:04:00.430 --> 00:04:02.960
It doesn't stop at Iserlohn.

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:05.500
It may also mean the life or 
death of the Empire itself.

00:04:05.930 --> 00:04:08.530
You must take me to the commander at once.

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:12.980
<b>Episode 7</b>

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:12.980
<b>The Capture of Iserlohn (Part 2)</b>

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:18.490
A way to neutralize Iserlohn Fortress 
and infiltrate the Empire?

00:04:18.760 --> 00:04:19.740
Yes, sir.

00:04:19.740 --> 00:04:24.170
If it is true, the very purpose of 
Iserlohn Fortress will be lost.

00:04:24.170 --> 00:04:26.550
You don't need to tell me that!

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:29.150
Have you contacted the garrison?

00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:32.410
Our communications remain 
hindered by jamming signals.

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:37.130
And times like these are precisely 
when we need a garrison force...

00:04:37.620 --> 00:04:39.640
That pig-headed Seeckt!

00:04:41.230 --> 00:04:44.540
Ready the Thor Hammer and 
all cannons for battle.

00:04:44.540 --> 00:04:45.840
Understood, sir!

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:49.940
First of all, bring that ship's 
captain here at once.

00:04:49.940 --> 00:04:50.700
Yes, sir!

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:03.020
Once we've made it into enemy 
territory, what then?

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:05.970
Our strategy has one objective:

00:05:06.380 --> 00:05:09.670
to occupy the Iserlohn 
Fortress control room.

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:14.670
The problem is that, since the Alliance's 
map of the fortress is incomplete,

00:05:14.670 --> 00:05:17.840
we're unable to pinpoint the 
central control room's location.

00:05:18.320 --> 00:05:19.960
There are five possibilities.

00:05:21.350 --> 00:05:26.030
So we need to have the enemy 
take us to all of them.

00:05:26.030 --> 00:05:28.260
Yes, exactly.

00:05:28.510 --> 00:05:30.490
And if we can accomplish that,

00:05:30.490 --> 00:05:34.120
we can take down any fortress, 
no matter how impregnable.

00:05:34.950 --> 00:05:37.310
The same could be said of a woman's heart.

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:41.440
That's all very easy to say, 
but difficult to do.

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:48.720
The nearest potential location is 
approximately 7,300 meters from the port.

00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:52.110
The farthest is 21,600 meters away.

00:05:52.640 --> 00:05:57.110
We will have to cover that much distance 
in a fortress full of enemies.

00:05:57.620 --> 00:05:59.470
This will be the second hurdle.

00:06:00.270 --> 00:06:02.610
It's going to call for 
some acting skill, then.

00:06:02.610 --> 00:06:03.520
Yes.

00:06:15.500 --> 00:06:16.690
<i>Walter,</i>

00:06:16.910 --> 00:06:19.920
<i>what do you want to be when you grow up?</i>

00:06:19.920 --> 00:06:23.160
<i>What do you mean? I'm a noble.</i>

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:24.590
<i>A noble...</i>

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:26.330
<i>True.</i>

00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:29.100
<i>And does that mean you 
can't be anything else?</i>

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:34.940
What's that on your arm?

00:06:36.220 --> 00:06:37.660
It appears to be a tattoo.

00:06:38.540 --> 00:06:41.990
Tattoos on Imperial soldiers are 
strictly forbidden by military law.

00:06:42.690 --> 00:06:44.960
No, this is...

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:47.200
It's for our espionage mission.

00:06:47.820 --> 00:06:53.070
It was necessary in order to blend in 
with the rebels and gain information.

00:06:53.760 --> 00:06:57.070
Of course, it will be removed 
once this mission is over.

00:06:57.630 --> 00:07:00.950
I see. Please forgive my indiscretion.

00:07:01.350 --> 00:07:01.970
Not at all.

00:07:10.260 --> 00:07:13.500
I am Lieutenant Commander Remler, 
captain of the control room guard.

00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:13.950
<u>Iserlohn Fortress Control Room Guard Captain
</u>Lieutenant Commander Remler

00:07:13.940 --> 00:07:17.440
I will take you to the commander from here.

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:21.310
Firearms may not be carried 
into the control room.

00:07:21.310 --> 00:07:24.830
You will leave any guns 
you're carrying here.

00:07:24.830 --> 00:07:28.800
Then, you will be examined by the 
full-body scanner over there.

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:32.770
No exceptions, even if you're operating
under the fleet admiral's orders.

00:07:33.470 --> 00:07:35.720
The third hurdle will be the body check.

00:07:36.040 --> 00:07:39.180
It's impossible to carry any weapons 
into the central control room.

00:07:39.690 --> 00:07:42.150
You will be put through thorough checks.

00:07:44.600 --> 00:07:46.600
So, what do we do?

00:08:09.250 --> 00:08:10.190
Hold it!

00:08:13.230 --> 00:08:14.440
Pardon me.

00:08:22.520 --> 00:08:24.300
It belonged to my grandfather.

00:08:25.300 --> 00:08:27.970
I keep it on my person at all times.

00:08:27.970 --> 00:08:29.610
It protects me.

00:08:30.750 --> 00:08:31.910
Is that all right?

00:08:33.620 --> 00:08:34.500
Thank you.

00:08:35.570 --> 00:08:38.900
Finally, I'll need to see your IDs.

00:08:38.900 --> 00:08:41.620
We sent those to you when we entered port.

00:08:42.030 --> 00:08:43.850
These are the rules.

00:08:51.790 --> 00:08:53.440
Verification failure.

00:08:54.440 --> 00:08:56.890
I can't allow you to 
enter the control room.

00:08:57.230 --> 00:09:00.340
That's odd. Could there be a 
problem with the machine?

00:09:00.820 --> 00:09:02.770
I'll check back home.

00:09:02.770 --> 00:09:04.560
Wait here for a bit.

00:09:04.850 --> 00:09:06.110
You would waste that much time?

00:09:06.110 --> 00:09:08.650
We don't know when the 
transmission will even work!

00:09:11.480 --> 00:09:12.510
Very well.

00:09:13.170 --> 00:09:15.730
I'd be glad to wait a month or two.

00:09:19.370 --> 00:09:20.660
What are you doing?!

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:23.210
His Excellency demands haste!

00:09:23.210 --> 00:09:24.190
But we have—

00:09:23.690 --> 00:09:25.820
Just bring them in at once!

00:09:28.440 --> 00:09:29.950
Understood.

00:09:34.710 --> 00:09:35.800
Where are they?

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:38.350
Finally.

00:09:39.160 --> 00:09:40.650
Explain what's going on!

00:09:41.480 --> 00:09:44.160
In order to take the commander hostage,

00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:47.250
you'll need to acquire a weapon 
inside the control room.

00:09:48.670 --> 00:09:52.100
You'll borrow it from 
the commander himself.

00:09:52.560 --> 00:09:57.580
In other words, you'll have only your 
own strength to rely on at this stage.

00:09:58.250 --> 00:10:02.530
I hate to ask this of you, 
but can you do it?

00:10:07.370 --> 00:10:08.370
Oh...

00:10:08.760 --> 00:10:10.460
I think I can work something out.

00:10:14.860 --> 00:10:16.380
You really are a rebel, aren't you?!

00:10:19.600 --> 00:10:20.880
You—

00:10:30.280 --> 00:10:34.140
Your Excellency Stockhausen, 
you are now our prisoner.

00:10:34.140 --> 00:10:35.220
Your Excellency!

00:10:37.380 --> 00:10:39.560
Who the hell are you people?!

00:10:39.830 --> 00:10:41.600
Pleased to make your acquaintance.

00:10:41.920 --> 00:10:47.030
I am Captain Schönkopf of the Rosen Ritter, 
a regiment of the Free Planets Alliance.

00:10:49.890 --> 00:10:51.680
The Rosen Ritter?

00:10:52.240 --> 00:10:54.170
I've heard of you.

00:10:54.170 --> 00:10:56.920
You're a band of traitors 
who abandoned the Empire!

00:10:56.920 --> 00:11:00.120
I'm so honored to know you've heard of us.

00:11:00.120 --> 00:11:03.200
Don't put Imperial soldiers on 
the same level as you bastards!

00:11:03.200 --> 00:11:06.090
Our commander fears dishonor 
more than death!

00:11:07.760 --> 00:11:11.090
He doesn't seem to appreciate you 
overestimating him like that.

00:11:13.960 --> 00:11:15.010
What did you do?!

00:11:16.290 --> 00:11:20.220
The last hurdle will be how thoroughly 
you can occupy the control room.

00:11:20.440 --> 00:11:26.050
I doubt that just taking the commander 
hostage will be enough to fully take it over.

00:11:26.050 --> 00:11:27.200
True.

00:11:27.570 --> 00:11:29.190
Then, what should we do?

00:11:30.060 --> 00:11:33.160
Karl Seffle, a practitioner 
of applied chemistry,

00:11:33.390 --> 00:11:39.330
invented a chemical for use in 
mining and civil engineering on a planetary scale.

00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:43.670
It's something like a gas that combusts in

00:11:43.670 --> 00:11:46.830
reaction to heat and energy 
exceeding a certain level.

00:11:47.990 --> 00:11:49.760
Seffle particles?

00:11:49.760 --> 00:11:52.150
Yes, Seffle particles.

00:11:52.670 --> 00:11:54.460
I'll take some into the room.

00:11:54.460 --> 00:11:55.480
But...

00:11:55.820 --> 00:11:58.080
Using it in normal close-range 
combat would be one thing,

00:11:58.080 --> 00:12:02.690
but using it in a raid like this is 
likely to produce unexpected results.

00:12:02.690 --> 00:12:06.810
You could all be caught in 
the explosion and die!

00:12:07.270 --> 00:12:10.450
If you have any other suggestions, 
I'd love to hear them.

00:12:11.220 --> 00:12:15.450
You have known all this time 
that there is no other way.

00:12:16.260 --> 00:12:20.160
Well, I wanted to keep trying 
to come up with a safer way

00:12:20.160 --> 00:12:22.170
until the last possible minute.

00:12:23.550 --> 00:12:28.590
I just pray that trusting heart of yours 
doesn't claim your life one day.

00:12:31.590 --> 00:12:33.740
If you fire, the particles will ignite,

00:12:33.740 --> 00:12:36.710
and everyone in here will 
be blown to space dust.

00:12:37.100 --> 00:12:38.650
Seffle particles?

00:12:39.310 --> 00:12:41.330
D-Don't do something so foolish!

00:12:41.730 --> 00:12:44.660
Doesn't the blood of the Empire 
flow through your veins, too?!

00:12:45.090 --> 00:12:49.040
If you surrender now, we're willing
to make you an excellent offer!

00:12:49.460 --> 00:12:51.700
Oh? Do you mean that?

00:12:52.600 --> 00:12:55.160
Ninety minutes have passed since 
the task force's infiltration.

00:12:55.810 --> 00:12:58.380
That's far longer than we anticipated.

00:12:58.740 --> 00:13:00.860
I hate to think it,

00:13:00.860 --> 00:13:04.150
but could he have become 
the seventh traitor?

00:13:04.150 --> 00:13:08.890
If that were the case, the enemy 
would have taken us all by now.

00:13:09.980 --> 00:13:14.190
Captain Schönkopf accepted the 
most dangerous role of all.

00:13:14.580 --> 00:13:17.390
I will honor my own word and trust him.

00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:21.630
That is quite the attractive offer,

00:13:21.630 --> 00:13:23.970
but I'll have to refuse this time.

00:13:23.970 --> 00:13:28.200
I need to honor my word to a man 
who said he would trust me.

00:13:28.690 --> 00:13:33.980
Besides, there are still lots of girls in 
the Alliance that I haven't seduced yet!

00:13:34.230 --> 00:13:36.040
Then you'll die with us!

00:13:36.360 --> 00:13:37.990
Have it your way.

00:13:42.350 --> 00:13:43.910
Don't, Remler!

00:13:44.260 --> 00:13:45.440
Th-That's enough!

00:13:45.890 --> 00:13:46.880
But, sir...

00:13:47.330 --> 00:13:51.210
You win. We surrender.

00:13:51.210 --> 00:13:52.590
You heard him.

00:13:55.040 --> 00:13:55.800
Damn it!

00:13:57.350 --> 00:13:59.420
A wise decision.

00:14:10.010 --> 00:14:13.510
There is nothing to be done. It's 
meaningless to discuss it.

00:14:13.900 --> 00:14:17.860
A noble of fine lineage grew so 
power-hungry that he used his wiles

00:14:18.210 --> 00:14:21.090
to steal our family's entire fortune.

00:14:21.500 --> 00:14:25.050
On top of that, he brought a warrant 
for my arrest on the grounds

00:14:25.050 --> 00:14:27.590
of thought crimes against the emperor.

00:14:28.430 --> 00:14:30.260
What will you do?

00:14:30.610 --> 00:14:33.470
Now, there's nothing to worry about.

00:14:34.430 --> 00:14:38.420
We will seek asylum with the 
Free Planets Alliance.

00:14:38.670 --> 00:14:41.070
Free Planets Alliance?

00:14:44.820 --> 00:14:45.800
Captain.

00:14:46.630 --> 00:14:48.830
I wiped off the blood, but...

00:14:49.120 --> 00:14:50.780
It's fine. Thank you.

00:14:51.720 --> 00:14:54.210
It was important to you, wasn't it?

00:14:54.210 --> 00:14:54.990
Hey, come on.

00:14:55.350 --> 00:14:59.450
You have to throw at least one 
truth in with any false story.

00:14:59.750 --> 00:15:03.580
Men are one thing, but women will 
always catch you otherwise.

00:15:15.580 --> 00:15:17.470
Forgive me, Captain.

00:15:17.790 --> 00:15:19.880
I doubted you.

00:15:20.280 --> 00:15:22.190
I thought you might betray us.

00:15:22.190 --> 00:15:26.320
Hey, having people suspect 
me is part of my job.

00:15:26.670 --> 00:15:28.220
It doesn't bother me.

00:15:29.520 --> 00:15:30.700
Admiral, sir.

00:15:31.460 --> 00:15:33.060
Great work.

00:15:33.670 --> 00:15:36.860
As planned, we've pumped sleeping 
gas throughout the fortress

00:15:36.860 --> 00:15:38.540
via the air conditioning system.

00:15:39.070 --> 00:15:42.700
When they wake up, all 500,000 
of them will be our prisoners.

00:15:43.590 --> 00:15:45.410
I guess it really did work out.

00:15:46.550 --> 00:15:48.380
It would seem so.

00:15:54.900 --> 00:15:56.010
What?!

00:15:56.370 --> 00:15:58.470
A revolt inside the fortress?!

00:15:58.470 --> 00:16:00.920
Yes, sir. A revolt has broken 
out among some soldiers.

00:16:00.920 --> 00:16:03.090
Immediate aid has been requested.

00:16:03.480 --> 00:16:06.520
Can't he even keep his 
subordinates under control?

00:16:06.520 --> 00:16:08.530
Stockhausen, you incompetent fool!

00:16:09.270 --> 00:16:11.750
We must first stamp out 
the fire at our feet.

00:16:11.750 --> 00:16:14.100
We will return to Iserlohn at once!

00:16:14.650 --> 00:16:16.090
Please wait.

00:16:17.520 --> 00:16:21.430
I don't recall asking for your 
opinion, Captain Oberstein!

00:16:21.430 --> 00:16:25.830
I am aware of that, 
but I will give it anyway.

00:16:25.830 --> 00:16:27.530
This is a trap.

00:16:27.530 --> 00:16:31.770
It seems everything is a trap in your eyes!

00:16:31.770 --> 00:16:34.260
Your Excellency, please listen to me.

00:16:34.260 --> 00:16:35.230
Enough!

00:16:35.640 --> 00:16:37.280
All fleets, turn around!

00:16:37.280 --> 00:16:39.980
Head for Iserlohn at combat speed two!

00:16:40.330 --> 00:16:43.330
This is a good opportunity to make 
those space moles indebted to us!

00:16:43.730 --> 00:16:47.570
<i>He isn't even suspicious about why 
communications are working again</i>

00:16:47.570 --> 00:16:49.600
<i>after they'd been disrupted for so long?</i>

00:16:50.360 --> 00:16:53.370
<i>There's no talking to such 
a small-minded bastard,</i>

00:16:53.780 --> 00:16:55.430
<i>full of anger and no courage.</i>

00:17:04.590 --> 00:17:07.050
Enemy fleet has entered firing range.

00:17:09.410 --> 00:17:12.900
Energy charge to the fortress's 
main cannon is complete.

00:17:14.180 --> 00:17:17.070
Aim is set. Ready to fire at any time.

00:17:22.800 --> 00:17:24.760
Change the main cannon's angle.

00:17:25.130 --> 00:17:26.560
Elevation: seven degrees.

00:17:28.220 --> 00:17:34.020
Forgive me, but at that angle, the shot 
will only graze the enemy's left flank.

00:17:34.020 --> 00:17:36.230
That's fine. Do it.

00:17:38.210 --> 00:17:38.980
Fire.

00:17:54.800 --> 00:17:56.240
Why are they firing on their allies?!

00:17:56.240 --> 00:17:58.740
No... It must be the rebels!

00:17:58.740 --> 00:18:00.960
What do we do?! We can't fire back!

00:18:00.960 --> 00:18:02.770
How do we escape the main cannon?!

00:18:04.610 --> 00:18:06.210
Have you gone mad?

00:18:06.730 --> 00:18:08.940
What are you fools doing?! Return fire!

00:18:08.940 --> 00:18:10.480
All fleets, salvo fire 
from the main cannons!

00:18:22.070 --> 00:18:23.740
Change the main cannon's angle.

00:18:24.140 --> 00:18:26.130
Aim for the enemy fleet's right flank.

00:18:28.890 --> 00:18:29.580
Fire.

00:18:38.470 --> 00:18:42.420
This can't be called a battle, Admiral.

00:18:42.730 --> 00:18:44.790
It's a one-sided massacre.

00:18:45.260 --> 00:18:47.900
Yes. You're right.

00:18:48.750 --> 00:18:51.850
We don't need to do the evil things 
that the Imperial Navy does.

00:18:52.380 --> 00:18:55.450
Advise them to surrender.

00:18:55.890 --> 00:18:58.080
If they refuse, advise them to flee.

00:18:58.080 --> 00:19:00.090
We won't pursue.

00:19:02.490 --> 00:19:03.940
Message from Iserlohn.

00:19:04.240 --> 00:19:06.660
"The Alliance has occupied Iserlohn."

00:19:06.660 --> 00:19:07.910
The Alliance...

00:19:07.910 --> 00:19:10.300
"Further bloodshed will benefit no one.

00:19:10.300 --> 00:19:11.480
Surrender."

00:19:11.480 --> 00:19:13.100
Surrender?!

00:19:13.100 --> 00:19:17.580
Also... "If you refuse to surrender, 
then flee. We will not pursue.

00:19:18.030 --> 00:19:20.870
Alliance Navy Rear Admiral Yang Wen-li."

00:19:22.400 --> 00:19:23.590
Your Excellency!

00:19:23.590 --> 00:19:26.030
We've confirmed an Alliance 
fleet behind us!

00:19:26.030 --> 00:19:28.070
We'll be caught in a pincer attack!

00:19:28.070 --> 00:19:29.640
A pincer attack?!

00:19:29.640 --> 00:19:31.670
Your Excellency, what shall we do?!

00:19:32.780 --> 00:19:36.120
We cannot surrender to the rebels!

00:19:36.600 --> 00:19:40.400
Facing the kaiser after losing the fortress

00:19:40.400 --> 00:19:42.970
would be a crime worse than 
ten thousand deaths!

00:19:43.510 --> 00:19:45.930
"You fail to understand 
the heart of a warrior.

00:19:45.930 --> 00:19:49.010
We know the path of dying 
to preserve our honor,

00:19:49.010 --> 00:19:51.710
and we know not the path 
of living in disgrace.

00:19:52.250 --> 00:19:55.230
All of our ships will henceforth 
charge into an honorable death.

00:19:55.230 --> 00:19:58.200
This is the only way to repay 
our kaiser's favor toward us."

00:19:58.620 --> 00:20:00.660
The heart of a warrior?

00:20:00.960 --> 00:20:03.300
All enemy ships are charging!

00:20:05.860 --> 00:20:07.920
Can you identify the enemy's flagship?

00:20:07.920 --> 00:20:08.890
Yes, sir.

00:20:08.890 --> 00:20:11.590
Then focus all of our fire on it.

00:20:11.930 --> 00:20:13.570
This will be our final bombardment.

00:20:14.120 --> 00:20:17.040
If the flagship is lost, the others will flee.

00:20:22.340 --> 00:20:23.130
Fire.

00:20:37.820 --> 00:20:39.640
Enemy flagship destroyed.

00:20:39.640 --> 00:20:42.530
All other ships are turning 
and leaving the front.

00:20:44.830 --> 00:20:46.380
Sub-lieutenant Greenhill.

00:20:46.380 --> 00:20:47.310
Yes, sir?

00:20:47.310 --> 00:20:49.780
Contact the Alliance.

00:20:49.780 --> 00:20:53.970
Tell them, "It's over. If you ask 
me to do it again, I can't."

00:20:54.510 --> 00:20:57.140
Take care of the rest. I'm beat.

00:20:57.610 --> 00:20:58.970
Understood.

00:21:02.780 --> 00:21:05.100
The heart of a warrior, indeed.

00:21:05.100 --> 00:21:07.970
It's because of men like him 
that this war won't end.

00:21:07.970 --> 00:21:10.650
I'm sick of being involved with that type.

00:21:21.160 --> 00:21:24.130
<i>Does this make me a cowardly runaway?</i>

00:21:24.820 --> 00:21:30.820
<i>I'll be the ideal target of blame for anyone 
who's only interested in self-preservation.</i>

00:21:35.740 --> 00:21:37.000
<i>Now, then...</i>

00:21:40.270 --> 00:21:44.900
Dominion of Fezzan

00:21:41.360 --> 00:21:45.190
Oh? So Iserlohn has fallen 
into the Alliance's hands?

00:21:45.570 --> 00:21:48.650
That is correct, Landesherr.

00:21:49.430 --> 00:21:52.650
I never expected them to be successful.

00:21:53.220 --> 00:21:57.670
Yang Wen-li is quite an intriguing man.

00:21:58.120 --> 00:22:01.450
Contact Heinessen and collect 
information on him at once.

00:21:58.710 --> 00:22:02.590
Nicholas Boltik

00:22:01.450 --> 00:22:02.180
Sir.

00:22:02.590 --> 00:22:06.880
It would seem wise to learn 
what kind of man he is.

00:22:08.300 --> 00:22:12.060
<u>Dominion of Fezzan Leader
</u>Adrian Rubinsky

00:23:43.610 --> 00:23:45.920
"Recently, Iserlohn Fortress,

00:23:45.920 --> 00:23:49.920
for which we had resigned ourselves to 
many long years of blood and tears,

00:23:49.920 --> 00:23:53.530
was brought down with zero 
losses on our side.

00:23:53.910 --> 00:23:56.560
The brilliantly intuitive strategy 
that brought us this result

00:23:56.560 --> 00:24:01.490
makes this man truly worthy of being called 
'Magician Yang' and 'Miracle Yang'."

00:24:01.870 --> 00:24:03.010
Hear that?

00:24:03.480 --> 00:24:04.970
Honestly...

00:24:05.240 --> 00:24:07.330
They have no idea what I went through.

00:24:08.030 --> 00:24:11.250
Still, this means my work is done.

00:24:12.630 --> 00:24:15.630
Now I can proudly request to 
retire from the service.

00:24:15.630 --> 00:24:20.060
Retirement aside, you've 
earned everyone's praise.

00:24:22.080 --> 00:24:24.430
Why don't you just let yourself enjoy it?

00:24:26.650 --> 00:24:29.250
I'll only be praised as 
long as I'm winning.

00:24:29.670 --> 00:24:32.400
If I continue to fight, 
I'll lose eventually.

00:24:32.880 --> 00:24:35.610
From anyone else's perspective,

00:24:35.610 --> 00:24:38.160
it'd be fun to see how their 
attitudes change then.

00:24:39.800 --> 00:24:41.390
By the way, Julian...

00:24:41.390 --> 00:24:43.030
Yes? What is it?

00:24:43.630 --> 00:24:46.930
Can't you at least let me drink 
my brandy when I want to?

00:24:50.010 --> 00:25:00.010
<b>Episode 8</b>

00:24:50.010 --> 00:25:00.010
<b>The Castrop Rebellion</b>

00:24:50.410 --> 00:24:54.980
<i>Next time on </i>Legend of 
 the Galactic Heroes - Die Neue These<i>,</i>

00:24:54.980 --> 00:24:58.810
<i>episode eight, "The Castrop Rebellion."</i>
